---
/*
 * The first outside test, in the tester's own words.
 *
 * One voice, set as one voice. The instinct with a testimonial section is a
 * grid of three cards, and with a single report that grid either sits
 * two-thirds empty or gets padded out with things somebody did not quite say.
 * Nothing here pretends to be a chorus: it is one person, named, on one
 * distribution, and the section says so underneath rather than leaving the
 * reader to assume a volume of praise that does not exist.
 *
 * The quotes are verbatim, capitals included. "REALLY" and "FLAWLESS" are his
 * emphasis, not a designer's, and leaving them as typed is the difference
 * between a quotation and a rewrite. It also happens to be the tell that these
 * are somebody's actual messages rather than copy written to sound like them.
 *
 * The line about the bug he found stays in. A testimonial that reports a clean
 * sweep is less believable than one that does not, and this page's whole
 * argument is that its claims are checkable.
 */

/* Verbatim, from the messages. Do not tidy the capitals. */
const quote =
  'I was REALLY trying to find something that bugs me or irritates or is somewhat not working… found pretty much nothing.'
const second = 'Everything in my experience on my Debian machine has been FLAWLESS.'

const person = {
  name: 'Artto Aunap',
  role: 'GNU/Linux automation developer',
  url: 'https://artto.name',
  /* For the monogram. Two letters, because a circle is not a nameplate. */
  initials: 'AA',
}
---

<section id="testimonial" class="wrap">
  <figure class="block">
    <blockquote>
      <p class="lead">{quote}</p>
      <p class="second">{second}</p>
    </blockquote>

    <figcaption class="by">
      {
        /*
        A monogram rather than a photo for now. The avatar is the one element
        here that is not load-bearing: the name, the role and the link do the
        attributing, and a circle with two letters in it reads as a person
        without the page depending on an image to say so.
      */
      }
      <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">{person.initials}</span>

      <span class="who">
        <a class="name" href={person.url} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          {person.name}
        </a>
        <span class="role">{person.role}</span>
      </span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p class="note">
    The first test of rigseed by somebody other than its author, run on Debian. He also found one
    layout fault in the speed limits dialog, which is the half of the report that was actually worth
    having.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .block {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    /* A rule above and below rather than a card. The section is a held breath
       between the theming demonstration and the download, and a bordered box
       would make it one more panel in a page that already has several. */
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  .lead {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: 'Archivo', 'Inter Variable', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 2.1rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .second {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 46ch;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .by {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .avatar {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2.5rem;
    height: 2.5rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface2);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: 'Archivo', 'Inter Variable', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .who {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .name {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
    width: fit-content;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color var(--t-fast) ease;
  }

  .name:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .role {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-dimmer);
  }

  .note {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-dimmer);
  }
</style>
